&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TextRun SCXW267002851 BCX0&quot; lang=&quot;EN-US&quot; data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW267002851 BCX0&quot;&gt;This position will be open until it is successfully filled. To &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW267002851 BCX0&quot;&gt;submit&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW267002851 BCX0&quot;&gt; your application, please follow the directions below.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TextRun MacChromeBold SCXW267002851 BCX0&quot; lang=&quot;EN-US&quot; data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW267002851 BCX0&quot;&gt;#LI-Onsite&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;To conform to U.S. Government space technology export regulations, including the International Traffic in Arms Regulations (ITAR) you must be a U.S. citizen, lawful permanent resident of the U.S., protected individual as defined by 8 U.S.C. 1324b(a)(3), or eligible to obtain the required authorizations from the U.S. Department of State.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;True Anomaly is committed to equal employment opportunity on any basis protected by applicable state and federal laws. If you have a disability or additional need that requires accommodation, please do not hesitate to let us know.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To protect candidates and our company from application fraud and impersonation, we use third-party tools to verify applicant identity and detect fraudulent applications. Learn more in our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.trueanomaly.space/legal/privacy-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;Space is a warfighting domain. True Anomaly seeks those with the talent and ambition to build the technology that secures it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;OUR MISSION&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;True Anomaly delivers decisive capabilities for space superiority. We build autonomous spacecraft, advanced payloads, mission software, and space-based interceptors — enabling the U.S. and its Allies to secure the space environment and counter threats from the ultimate high ground.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;OUR VALUES&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be the offset.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;We create asymmetric advantages with creativity and ingenuity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What would it take?&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;We challenge assumptions to deliver ambitious results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;It’s the people.&lt;/strong&gt; Our team is our competitive advantage and we are better together.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;BENEFITS &amp;amp; PERKS&lt;/span&gt;*&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Best-in-class healthcare: &lt;/strong&gt;100% company-paid medical, dental, and vision coverage for you and your dependents, with HSA/HRA options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Generous time off: &lt;/strong&gt;Flexible Time Off (FTO) for exempt employees, accrued PTO of up to 25 days for non-exempt employees, plus 12 paid holidays; Parental Leave; Sick Leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fuel for your day: &lt;/strong&gt;Daily catered lunch and unlimited snacks for in-office employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;And more: &lt;/strong&gt;401(k) retirement plan, fitness reimbursement, and Dog Fridays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity participation: &lt;/strong&gt;Equity is included as part of our total compensation package, giving you an opportunity to share in the company’s success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*Do not apply to fixed term and temporary roles&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;YOUR MISSION&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Contracts Manager will serve as a member of the Prime Contracts Function, supporting U.S. Department of Defense and Intelligence Community (IC) contracts throughout the acquisition lifecycle—from proposal support through award, post-award performance, and closeout. Reporting to the Sr. Manager, Contracts, this role will work closely with program managers, engineering, finance, and legal to ensure contracts are properly structured, administered, and closed in compliance with applicable regulations and company policies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on role in a small, growing Contracts department. You will manage an assigned portfolio of contracts with support from the Sr. Manager, Contracts and serve as a key point of contact with government Contracting Officers and Contracting Officer Representatives. The ideal candidate brings practical government contracts experience, sound judgment, and the initiative to operate effectively in a lean organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pre-Award&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support proposal development, including preparation of representations and certifications, review of terms and conditions, and input on cost and pricing volumes from a contract’s perspective.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Award and Negotiation&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and support negotiation of contract terms and FAR/DFARS clauses with government Contracting Officers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with identifying, evaluating, and resolving contractual and business risks during negotiations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate internal review and approval of contract documents prior to execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure contracts are properly recorded, distributed, and set up for performance tracking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the Sr. Manager, Contracts and Legal Department in preparing negotiation positions, risk summaries, and approval materials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Post-Award Administration&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a day-to-day point of contact with government Contracting Officers and CORs for assigned contracts, escalating material issues as appropriate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and support contract modifications, change orders, option exercises, incremental funding actions, and other post-award contract actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and manage CDRLs, deliverable schedules, and other contractual performance obligations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor contract performance for scope, funding, and schedule risks, including identification and escalation of issues such as scope creep, constructive changes, and unauthorized commitments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and submit contract correspondence, including requests for information, cure notice responses, show cause responses, requests for equitable adjustment, and other formal communications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure appropriate FAR/DFARS flowdowns in subcontracts and supplier agreements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with interpreting contract requirements and translating complex contracting concepts into practical guidance for internal stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Compliance and Audit Support&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain contract files in audit-ready condition in accordance with applicable record retention requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the initial point of contact for routine DCAA and DCMA interactions, audits, and information requests, with support from the Sr. Contracts Manager and Legal Department as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support compliance with cost accounting standards, Truth in Negotiations Act requirements, and other regulatory obligations applicable to government contractors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and ensure timely completion of compliance-driven reporting and filing obligations tied to contract performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain contract compliance checklists, calendars, and internal controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Closeout&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support contract closeout procedures, including final deliverable verification, property disposition, release of claims, deobligation of excess funds, and coordination with finance on final invoicing and reconciliation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track open closeout items and coordinate with internal stakeholders and government counterparts to support timely completion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain appropriate closeout documentation in the contract file.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;General&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain contract status reports, trackers, and dashboards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support continuous improvement of contracting processes, templates, and playbooks within the Legal Department.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain strong working relationships with internal stakeholders across programs, engineering, finance, business development, and legal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take ownership of assigned projects and contract administration workstreams, contributing to the continued development of the company’s contracts function.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with additional projects and initiatives as needed under the direction of the General Counsel or Sr. Contracts Manager.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The successful candidate will be a proactive and energetic Contracts professional who combines hands-on DoD and/or IC contract administration experience with strong organizational skills, sound judgment, and the ability to work collaboratively across a growing company. Strong interpersonal skills are essential: this role requires close collaboration with program managers, engineers, finance, and other non-contracts stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in DoD and/or IC contract administration, with experience supporting government contracts through multiple stages of the acquisition lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active U.S. security clearance required (TS minimum, TS/SCI preferred).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience serving as a contracts point of contact with government Contracting Officers, Contracting Officer Representatives, or other government stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting, coordinating, or leading contract administration workstreams, with demonstrated readiness to take on increasing responsibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong working knowledge of the FAR, DFARS, and applicable agency-specific regulatory supplements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with one or more government contract types, including firm-fixed-price, OTAs, cost-plus-fixed-fee, cost-plus-award-fee, time-and-materials, and indefinite-delivery/indefinite-quantity contracts, and the ability to understand and communicate the practical implications of each.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with contract modifications, change orders, funding actions, REAs, and/or contract closeout.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently, prioritize effectively, exercise sound judgment, and communicate directly with government counterparts while knowing when to escalate issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, with experience drafting formal contract correspondence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to translate complex contracting concepts and requirements into practical guidance for non-contracts stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with contract management systems and tools, SAM.gov, and Microsoft Office.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience at an aerospace and/or defense company, and/or with DoD or IC contracts is strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a small company, startup, or high-growth environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting programs involving classified information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with DCAA and DCMA audit and oversight processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COMPENSATION&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-leveltext=&quot;&quot; data-font=&quot;Symbol&quot; data-listid=&quot;2&quot; data-list-defn-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335552541&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:720,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:360,&amp;quot;469769226&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;Symbol&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469769242&amp;quot;:[8226],&amp;quot;469777803&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;left&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777804&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777815&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;hybridMultilevel&amp;quot;}&quot; data-aria-posinset=&quot;1&quot; data-aria-level=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Base Salary:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:160,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt; $120,000 - $160,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:160,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TextRun SCXW83253800 BCX0&quot; lang=&quot;EN-US&quot; data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW83253800 BCX0&quot;&gt;Your actual level and base salary will be&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW83253800 BCX0&quot;&gt;determined&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW83253800 BCX0&quot;&gt; on a case-by-case basis and may vary based on the following considerations: job-related knowledge and skills, education, location, and experience.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;EOP SCXW83253800 BCX0&quot; data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Location&lt;/strong&gt;—Successful candidates will be located near Centennial, CO. While we observe a hybrid work environment, some work must be done on site.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TextRun SCXW267002851 BCX0&quot; lang=&quot;EN-US&quot; data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW267002851 BCX0&quot;&gt;This position will be open until it is successfully filled. To &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW267002851 BCX0&quot;&gt;submit&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW267002851 BCX0&quot;&gt; your application, please follow the directions below.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TextRun MacChromeBold SCXW267002851 BCX0&quot; lang=&quot;EN-US&quot; data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW267002851 BCX0&quot;&gt;#LI-Onsite&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;To conform to U.S. Government space technology export regulations, including the International Traffic in Arms Regulations (ITAR) you must be a U.S. citizen, lawful permanent resident of the U.S., protected individual as defined by 8 U.S.C. 1324b(a)(3), or eligible to obtain the required authorizations from the U.S. Department of State.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;True Anomaly is committed to equal employment opportunity on any basis protected by applicable state and federal laws. If you have a disability or additional need that requires accommodation, please do not hesitate to let us know.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To protect candidates and our company from application fraud and impersonation, we use third-party tools to verify applicant identity and detect fraudulent applications. Learn more in our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.trueanomaly.space/legal/privacy-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;Space is a warfighting domain. True Anomaly seeks those with the talent and ambition to build the technology that secures it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;OUR MISSION&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;True Anomaly delivers decisive capabilities for space superiority. We build autonomous spacecraft, advanced payloads, mission software, and space-based interceptors — enabling the U.S. and its Allies to secure the space environment and counter threats from the ultimate high ground.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;OUR VALUES&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be the offset.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;We create asymmetric advantages with creativity and ingenuity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What would it take?&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;We challenge assumptions to deliver ambitious results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;It’s the people.&lt;/strong&gt; Our team is our competitive advantage and we are better together.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;BENEFITS &amp;amp; PERKS&lt;/span&gt;*&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Best-in-class healthcare: &lt;/strong&gt;100% company-paid medical, dental, and vision coverage for you and your dependents, with HSA/HRA options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Generous time off: &lt;/strong&gt;Flexible Time Off (FTO) for exempt employees, accrued PTO of up to 25 days for non-exempt employees, plus 12 paid holidays; Parental Leave; Sick Leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fuel for your day: &lt;/strong&gt;Daily catered lunch and unlimited snacks for in-office employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;And more: &lt;/strong&gt;401(k) retirement plan, fitness reimbursement, and Dog Fridays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity participation: &lt;/strong&gt;Equity is included as part of our total compensation package, giving you an opportunity to share in the company’s success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*Do not apply to fixed term and temporary roles&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;YOUR MISSION&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Corporate Counsel, IP will serve as True Anomaly&#39;s primary in-house legal authority on intellectual property, owning the maturation and execution of the company&#39;s IP strategy — including how we identify, capture, protect, and leverage technology across both our hardware and software. This role reports to the Managing Counsel and is a key member of a small, collaborative legal department.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Intellectual property is the core of this role. You will lead the company&#39;s IP program, partnering closely with engineering, marketing, product, program management, business development, and mission teams to identify proprietary innovations and implement appropriate&amp;nbsp;protections the&amp;nbsp;company’s IP portfolios, negotiate and manage licenses, establish the practical processes that turn day-to-day engineering into defensible IP, and serve as the go-to resource for stakeholders across the company on strategy, ownership, and risk.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Beyond IP, you will support general corporate legal functions — reviewing and negotiating contracts, supporting transactional and financing needs, advising internal clients, and contributing to the legal&amp;nbsp;department’s&amp;nbsp;broader workload. The ideal candidate is energized by the opportunity to own and mature a specialized strategic function while also operating as a versatile member of a lean legal team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Intellectual Property&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Develop and own True Anomaly&#39;s IP strategy, including how the company identifies, captures, protects, and leverages inventions, patents, trade secrets, software, data, trademarks, and other proprietary technology.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Build and&amp;nbsp;manage&amp;nbsp;the practical infrastructure for IP: invention&amp;nbsp;mining&amp;nbsp;and disclosure processes, patent and trade secret decision-making,&amp;nbsp;trade secret protection practices, including identification, access controls, and documentation,&amp;nbsp;and clear guidance for engineers and software teams on protecting what they create.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the full lifecycle of the company’s patent and trademark portfolios, working with outside counsel on prosecution, prioritization, and budget.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Draft, negotiate, and manage inbound and outbound technology, software, data, and other IP license agreements.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Maintain systems for tracking license terms, obligations, renewals, and other key requirements.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Manage IP terms for employees, contractors, consultants, and other personnel, including proprietary information and invention assignment agreements (PIIAs) and prior-invention&amp;nbsp;disclosures.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Manage open-source and third-party software licensing compliance, including&amp;nbsp;copyleft and other licensing obligations.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Advise engineering, product, and program teams on&amp;nbsp;IP ownership, third-party rights, publication, invention disclosures, and other related matters.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Advise on IP and data rights in government contracts, including data rights assertions and markings and Bahy-Doyle obligations.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Partner with the export compliance&amp;nbsp;on issues involving&amp;nbsp;IP, technical data, and&amp;nbsp;ITAR/EAR&amp;nbsp;controls.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Monitor developments in IP law and policy that may affect the company&#39;s IP posture and proactively advise stakeholders.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;General Corporate Legal Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Draft, review, and negotiate a wide variety of agreements, including customer, partnership, and technology agreements, vendor and supplier contracts, program subcontracts, teaming agreements, NDAs, and consulting agreements.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise internal stakeholders across program management, systems engineering, communications and IT, mission operations, facilities management, security, finance, and supply chain on legal matters as they arise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with other Legal Department functions, including export compliance, on matters of overlapping regulatory concern.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to legal department process improvements, templates, playbooks, and other shared resources.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Support additional projects and initiatives as needed under the direction of the&amp;nbsp;Managing&amp;nbsp;Counsel.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;J.D. from an accredited law school and active bar membership in at least one U.S. jurisdiction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;3–7 years of legal experience,&amp;nbsp;preferably including both&amp;nbsp;law firm and in-house experience.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Experience&amp;nbsp;advising on&amp;nbsp;patents, trade secrets, software, technology transactions, licensing, and IP ownership.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Experience drafting, reviewing, and negotiating commercial contracts and license agreements independently.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience advising on IP ownership, data rights, and licensing matters in a technology or product-development environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Ability to work effectively with technical teams and translate complex&amp;nbsp;legal&amp;nbsp;information and technical concepts into&amp;nbsp;practical guidance.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written communication skills, with the ability to produce precise, well-organized legal documents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong presentation skills and ability to distill complex legal concepts into clear, accessible reports and briefings for internal audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High attention to detail and ability to manage multiple projects and competing deadlines simultaneously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A generalist&#39;s range and instinct — comfort operating across multiple areas of law and picking up unfamiliar issues quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in the commercial space, aerospace, defense, or other deep-technology industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in-house at a technology or aerospace company, ideally a startup or high-growth environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with government IP and data-rights frameworks (FAR/DFARS, Bayh-Dole, SBIR/STTR).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with open-source software compliance and software licensing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with export controls.&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COMPENSATION&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-leveltext=&quot;&quot; data-font=&quot;Symbol&quot; data-listid=&quot;2&quot; data-list-defn-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335552541&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:720,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:360,&amp;quot;469769226&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;Symbol&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469769242&amp;quot;:[8226],&amp;quot;469777803&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;left&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777804&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777815&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;hybridMultilevel&amp;quot;}&quot; data-aria-posinset=&quot;1&quot; data-aria-level=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Base Salary:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:160,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt; $140,000 - $205,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
