&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;BENEFITS &amp;amp; PERKS&lt;/span&gt;*&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Best-in-class healthcare: &lt;/strong&gt;100% company-paid medical, dental, and vision coverage for you and your dependents, with HSA/HRA options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Generous time off: &lt;/strong&gt;Flexible Time Off (FTO) for exempt employees, accrued PTO of up to 25 days for non-exempt employees, plus 12 paid holidays; Parental Leave; Sick Leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fuel for your day: &lt;/strong&gt;Daily catered lunch and unlimited snacks for in-office employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;And more: &lt;/strong&gt;401(k) retirement plan, fitness reimbursement, and Dog Fridays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity participation: &lt;/strong&gt;Equity is included as part of our total compensation package, giving you an opportunity to share in the company’s success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*Do not apply to fixed term and temporary roles&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;YOUR MISSION&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Fixed Asset Accountant at True Anomaly, you will own the integrity, visibility, and control processes for the company’s fixed assets across our locations in Colorado, California, and the Washington, DC area. Sitting at the intersection of Finance, Operations, Facilities, Procurement, Information Technology, Engineering, Manufacturing, and other business teams, you will ensure that capital investments and other trackable assets are accurately recorded, properly tracked, and reported throughout their lifecycle.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is critical to building scalable fixed asset accounting and asset-tracking processes that support True Anomaly’s growth and operational complexity. You will maintain accurate asset records, reconcile fixed asset activity to the general ledger, support monthly and year-end close, monitor construction-in-progress and capital projects, coordinate physical inventories, and provide reliable reporting for internal stakeholders and auditors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a detail-oriented, highly accountable problem solver who can bring structure to complex, multi-location asset data and build strong partnerships across the organization. If you thrive in an environment where you can identify gaps, improve processes, establish effective controls, and take ownership of accurate financial and operational information, this role is for you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate and complete fixed asset records for all True Anomaly locations, including property, buildings, leasehold improvements, machinery, equipment, furniture, vehicles, technology, and other capital assets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Record and monitor fixed asset additions, transfers, disposals, retirements, impairments, and write-offs in accordance with True Anomaly policies and U.S. GAAP.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review capital expenditures and supporting documentation to determine whether costs should be capitalized or expensed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish asset records and maintain information such as asset identification number, location, department, custodian, acquisition date, in-service date, cost, useful life, and depreciation method.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Calculate, record, and reconcile monthly depreciation and amortization expense.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor construction-in-progress and other capital projects, including the timely transfer of completed projects to the appropriate fixed asset categories.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare monthly, quarterly, and annual fixed asset reports, schedules, roll-forwards, and management analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reconcile the fixed asset subledger to the general ledger and investigate and resolve discrepancies in a timely manner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate fixed asset accounting and tracking activities across True Anomaly’s locations in Colorado, California, and the Washington, DC area.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Facilities, Operations, Procurement, Information Technology, Engineering, Manufacturing, Real Estate, and other departments to track transfers, disposals, and changes in status.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate periodic physical inventories and audits of fixed assets at True Anomaly locations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain appropriate documentation and audit trails for capital purchases, disposals, transfers, and other fixed asset transactions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support internal and external audits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with the accounting and reporting of asset-related leases, tenant improvements, and other location-based capital projects, as applicable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review fixed asset transactions for compliance with capitalization thresholds, useful-life guidelines, approval requirements, and internal controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with annual budgeting, forecasting, and analysis of capital expenditures and depreciation expense.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the implementation, enhancement, and maintenance of fixed asset modules within True Anomaly’s ERP or accounting systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the accounting, tracking, and control of government-furnished property or customer-owned property, as applicable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform other accounting, reporting, and finance-related duties as assigned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, Business Administration, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least three years of progressive accounting experience, including direct experience with fixed asset accounting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of fixed asset accounting principles, capitalization policies, depreciation, disposals, impairments, and asset reconciliations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of U.S. GAAP and the ability to apply accounting policies consistently across multiple locations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting physical asset inventories, fixed asset audits, and asset verification processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong proficiency with Microsoft Excel, including pivot tables, lookups, conditional formulas, and data analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with an ERP or accounting system with fixed asset functionality. NetSuite is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent attention to detail and strong organizational and time-management skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage multiple priorities and meet recurring monthly, quarterly, and annual deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work effectively with employees and stakeholders across multiple True Anomaly locations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability and willingness to travel periodically to True Anomaly facilities to support physical inventories, audits, and asset verification activities, as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing fixed assets across multiple states, facilities, or business units.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with construction-in-progress accounting, leasehold improvements, capital project accounting, or asset-intensive organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with fixed asset tagging, barcode or RFID tracking systems, and physical inventory software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting year-end audits, internal control testing, or SOX-related processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with state and local property tax reporting related to fixed assets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with government-furnished or customer-owned property and familiarity with applicable FAR and DFARS requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience improving accounting processes, implementing ERP systems, or developing fixed asset reporting tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COMPENSATION&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
