&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TextRun SCXW267002851 BCX0&quot; lang=&quot;EN-US&quot; data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW267002851 BCX0&quot;&gt;This position will be open until it is successfully filled. To &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW267002851 BCX0&quot;&gt;submit&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW267002851 BCX0&quot;&gt; your application, please follow the directions below. #LI-Onsite&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;To conform to U.S. Government space technology export regulations, including the International Traffic in Arms Regulations (ITAR) you must be a U.S. citizen, lawful permanent resident of the U.S., protected individual as defined by 8 U.S.C. 1324b(a)(3), or eligible to obtain the required authorizations from the U.S. Department of State.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;True Anomaly is committed to equal employment opportunity on any basis protected by applicable state and federal laws. If you have a disability or additional need that requires accommodation, please do not hesitate to let us know.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To protect candidates and our company from application fraud and impersonation, we use third-party tools to verify applicant identity and detect fraudulent applications. Learn more in our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.trueanomaly.space/legal/privacy-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;Space is a warfighting domain. True Anomaly seeks those with the talent and ambition to build the technology that secures it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;OUR MISSION&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;True Anomaly delivers decisive capabilities for space superiority. We build autonomous spacecraft, advanced payloads, mission software, and space-based interceptors — enabling the U.S. and its Allies to secure the space environment and counter threats from the ultimate high ground.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;OUR VALUES&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be the offset.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;We create asymmetric advantages with creativity and ingenuity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What would it take?&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;We challenge assumptions to deliver ambitious results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;It’s the people.&lt;/strong&gt; Our team is our competitive advantage and we are better together.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;BENEFITS &amp;amp; PERKS&lt;/span&gt;*&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Best-in-class healthcare: &lt;/strong&gt;100% company-paid medical, dental, and vision coverage for you and your dependents, with HSA/HRA options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Generous time off: &lt;/strong&gt;Flexible Time Off (FTO) for exempt employees, accrued PTO of up to 25 days for non-exempt employees, plus 12 paid holidays; Parental Leave; Sick Leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fuel for your day: &lt;/strong&gt;Daily catered lunch and unlimited snacks for in-office employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;And more: &lt;/strong&gt;401(k) retirement plan, fitness reimbursement, and Dog Fridays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity participation: &lt;/strong&gt;Equity is included as part of our total compensation package, giving you an opportunity to share in the company’s success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*Do not apply to fixed term and temporary roles&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;YOUR MISSION &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;As a Fluids and Propulsion Technician, you will play a vital role in the assembly, integration, and testing of propulsion systems. You will collaborate with engineering,&amp;nbsp;manufacturing, and quality teams to bring innovative propulsion systems from early&amp;nbsp;development through flight readiness and production ramp. This role may be leveled from&amp;nbsp;Technician I to Technician III based on experience, skills, and demonstrated proficiency.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Fluids and Propulsion Assembly&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Build, install, and test fluids and propulsion hardware—&amp;nbsp;including thrusters, tanks, valves, manifolds, fluid lines, panels, trays, and harnessing—using engineering drawings, work instructions, an process documentation. Bend, flare, fit, route, and clean tubes to meet required standards. Disassemble and assemble valves and&amp;nbsp;other propulsion components.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Component Preparation and Handling&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Prepare, clean, preserve, and handle fluid and&amp;nbsp;pressure-system components with precision. Operate and maintain cleaning, purge,&amp;nbsp;pressure, and test equipment while ensuring safety, cleanliness, and traceability.&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;System Integration&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;: Work alongside engineering and quality teams to integrate fluids and&amp;nbsp;propulsion components and subsystems. Support checkouts, inspections,&amp;nbsp;troubleshooting, nonconformance resolution, and functional testing.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Testing and Validation&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Conduct and support fluids and propulsion tests, including proof,&amp;nbsp;leak, pressure, flow, functional, and qualification testing. Set up test hardware and&amp;nbsp;equipment, follow test procedures, and accurately record test data.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Safety and Compliance&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Follow protocols for hazardous materials, pressurized systems,&amp;nbsp;FOD prevention, ESD control, cleanroom operations, and other applicable safety and&amp;nbsp;quality requirements.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Continuous Improvement&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Support improvements to assembly processes, tooling, work&amp;nbsp;instructions, and manufacturing methods. Provide guidance and technical support to less&amp;nbsp;experienced technicians as appropriate for level.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Technical degree, certificate, apprenticeship, or equivalent training in aerospace,&amp;nbsp;mechanical, manufacturing, welding, or a related field.&lt;br&gt;• Relevant experience in the assembly, integration, and testing of aerospace fluids,&amp;nbsp;propulsion, pressure, or high-reliability systems.&lt;br&gt;• Experience building and integrating fluids panels and tray assemblies.&lt;br&gt;• Proficiency reading engineering drawings, schematics, process sheets, and work&amp;nbsp;instructions.&lt;br&gt;• Experience with tubing, fittings, valves, manifolds, pressure systems, or related&amp;nbsp;hardware.&lt;br&gt;• Experience working in ESD-sensitive, FOD-critical, and cleanroom environments.&lt;br&gt;• Ability to safely use hand tools, torque tools, precision measurement equipment,&amp;nbsp;and specialized assembly or test equipment.&lt;br&gt;• Ability to work autonomously and collaboratively in a multidisciplinary team.&lt;br&gt;• Strong written and verbal communication skills.&lt;br&gt;• Ability to lift 25 pounds and work in and around constrained or confined spaces.&lt;br&gt;• Ability to follow detailed procedures and accurately document completed work and&lt;br&gt;test results.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;LEVELING GUIDANCE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Technician I&lt;/em&gt;:&lt;/strong&gt; Develops proficiency in fluids and propulsion assembly, component&amp;nbsp;preparation, documentation, and testing while working under regular guidance. Typically&amp;nbsp;has 0–1 years of relevant experience or equivalent technical training.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Technician II:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; Independently performs a broad range of assembly, integration,&amp;nbsp;troubleshooting, and test activities. Typically has 1–3 years of relevant experience.&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technician III&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/em&gt; Performs complex assembly, integration, troubleshooting, and testing with&amp;nbsp;limited supervision. Serves as a technical resource for other technicians and supports&lt;br&gt;process development, qualification testing, and production ramp. Typically has 3+ years of&amp;nbsp;relevant experience or equivalent demonstrated proficiency.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Aerospace welding and brazing&lt;br&gt;• Orbital tube welding&lt;br&gt;• Tube bending, flaring, swaging, and precision fitting&lt;br&gt;• Experience with leak, proof, pressure, flow, or functional testing&lt;br&gt;• Experience with hazardous fluids, high-pressure gas, cryogenic, or vacuum systems&lt;br&gt;• Experience supporting spacecraft integration, qualification testing, or production&amp;nbsp;operations&lt;br&gt;• Relevant welding, brazing, cleanroom, hazardous materials, or pressure-system&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
