&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Location&lt;/strong&gt;—Successful candidates will be located near Denver or Long Beach.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work environment&lt;/strong&gt;—the work environment; temperature, noise level, inside or outside, or other factors that will affect the person&#39;s working conditions while performing the job.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Physical demands&lt;/strong&gt;—the physical demands of the job, including bending, sitting, lifting and driving.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TextRun SCXW267002851 BCX0&quot; lang=&quot;EN-US&quot; data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW267002851 BCX0&quot;&gt;This position will be open until it is successfully filled. To &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW267002851 BCX0&quot;&gt;submit&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW267002851 BCX0&quot;&gt; your application, please follow the directions below.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TextRun MacChromeBold SCXW267002851 BCX0&quot; lang=&quot;EN-US&quot; data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(224, 62, 45);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW267002851 BCX0&quot;&gt;#LI-Onsite&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;To conform to U.S. Government space technology export regulations, including the International Traffic in Arms Regulations (ITAR) you must be a U.S. citizen, lawful permanent resident of the U.S., protected individual as defined by 8 U.S.C. 1324b(a)(3), or eligible to obtain the required authorizations from the U.S. Department of State.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;True Anomaly is committed to equal employment opportunity on any basis protected by applicable state and federal laws. If you have a disability or additional need that requires accommodation, please do not hesitate to let us know.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To protect candidates and our company from application fraud and impersonation, we use third-party tools to verify applicant identity and detect fraudulent applications. Learn more in our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.trueanomaly.space/legal/privacy-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;Space is a warfighting domain. True Anomaly seeks those with the talent and ambition to build the technology that secures it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;OUR MISSION&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;True Anomaly delivers decisive capabilities for space superiority. We build autonomous spacecraft, advanced payloads, mission software, and space-based interceptors — enabling the U.S. and its Allies to secure the space environment and counter threats from the ultimate high ground.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;OUR VALUES&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be the offset.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;We create asymmetric advantages with creativity and ingenuity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What would it take?&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;We challenge assumptions to deliver ambitious results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;It’s the people.&lt;/strong&gt; Our team is our competitive advantage and we are better together.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;BENEFITS &amp;amp; PERKS&lt;/span&gt;*&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Best-in-class healthcare: &lt;/strong&gt;100% company-paid medical, dental, and vision coverage for you and your dependents, with HSA/HRA options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Generous time off: &lt;/strong&gt;Flexible Time Off (FTO) for exempt employees, accrued PTO of up to 25 days for non-exempt employees, plus 12 paid holidays; Parental Leave; Sick Leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fuel for your day: &lt;/strong&gt;Daily catered lunch and unlimited snacks for in-office employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;And more: &lt;/strong&gt;401(k) retirement plan, fitness reimbursement, and Dog Fridays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity participation: &lt;/strong&gt;Equity is included as part of our total compensation package, giving you an opportunity to share in the company’s success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*Do not apply to fixed term and temporary roles&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;YOUR MISSION&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Mechanical Spacecraft Technician, you will play a vital role in the assembly,&amp;nbsp;integration, and testing of spacecraft mechanical systems. You will collaborate with&amp;nbsp;engineering, manufacturing, and quality teams to build spacecraft hardware from early&amp;nbsp;development through environmental testing, flight readiness, and production ramp. This role may be leveled from Technician I to Technician III based on experience, skills, and&amp;nbsp;demonstrated proficiency.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Mechanical Assembly&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Build, install, and inspect spacecraft mechanical hardware—including primary and secondary structures, panels, brackets, payloads, mechanisms,&amp;nbsp;deployables, thermal hardware, fasteners, and support equipment—using engineering&lt;br&gt;drawings, work instructions, and process documentation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Component Preparation and Handling&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;: Prepare, clean, protect, and handle flight and&amp;nbsp;flight-like hardware. Perform precision assembly operations including torqueing, safety&amp;nbsp;wiring, staking, bonding, shimming, alignment, and mechanical fastening while&amp;nbsp;maintaining hardware traceability and configuration control.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Spacecraft Integration&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Support the integration of mechanical subsystems and&amp;nbsp;components into spacecraft structures. Install and route hardware, perform fit checks and&amp;nbsp;dimensional inspections, and support closeouts and access panel installation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Testing and Validation:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; Support mechanical functional testing, deployment testing,&amp;nbsp;alignment checks, mass properties measurements, vibration testing, acoustic testing,&amp;nbsp;thermal vacuum testing, and other environmental test activities. Set up test hardware and&lt;br&gt;fixtures, follow approved procedures, and accurately record results.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Inspection and Troubleshooting&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Perform visual, dimensional, and workmanship&amp;nbsp;inspections. Identify and document hardware discrepancies, support nonconformance&amp;nbsp;investigations, and work with engineering and quality teams to resolve assembly and integration issues.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Tooling and Ground Support Equipment&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Operate and maintain hand tools, torque tools,&amp;nbsp;precision measurement equipment, lifting equipment, assembly fixtures, and mechanical&amp;nbsp;ground-support equipment. Support the development and improvement of tooling and&amp;nbsp;work instructions.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Safety and Compliance&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Follow requirements for FOD prevention, ESD control, cleanroom&amp;nbsp;operations, hazardous materials, lifting and handling, contamination control, and safe&amp;nbsp;work around energized and flight hardware.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Continuous Improvement&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Provide feedback on assembly processes, drawings, work&amp;nbsp;instructions, tooling, and manufacturing methods to improve safety, quality, repeatability,&amp;nbsp;and schedule performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Technical degree, certificate, apprenticeship, or equivalent training in mechanical,&amp;nbsp;aerospace, manufacturing, or a related field.&lt;br&gt;• Relevant experience in spacecraft, aerospace, defense, automotive, precision&amp;nbsp;manufacturing, or other high-reliability mechanical assembly environments.&lt;br&gt;• Experience assembling and integrating mechanical structures, mechanisms,&amp;nbsp;brackets, panels, fasteners, or related hardware.&lt;br&gt;• Proficiency reading engineering drawings, schematics, work instructions, process&amp;nbsp;sheets, and assembly procedures.&lt;br&gt;• Experience using hand tools, torque tools, precision measurement equipment, and&amp;nbsp;mechanical test equipment.&lt;br&gt;• Experience with mechanical alignment, dimensional inspection, shimming,&amp;nbsp;bonding, staking, or safety wiring.&lt;br&gt;• Experience working in ESD-sensitive, FOD-critical, and cleanroom environments.&lt;br&gt;• Ability to follow detailed procedures and maintain accurate build, inspection, and&lt;br&gt;test documentation.&lt;br&gt;• Ability to work autonomously and collaboratively in a multidisciplinary team.&lt;br&gt;• Strong written and verbal communication skills.&lt;br&gt;• Ability to lift 25 pounds and work in and around constrained or confined spaces.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;LEVELING GUIDANCE&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technician I&lt;/strong&gt;: Develops proficiency in spacecraft mechanical assembly, hardware&amp;nbsp;handling, documentation, and inspection while working under regular guidance. Typically&amp;nbsp;has 0–1 years of relevant experience or equivalent technical training.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technician II:&lt;/strong&gt; Independently performs a broad range of mechanical assembly, integration,&amp;nbsp;inspection, and test activities. Troubleshoots common issues and supports process&amp;nbsp;improvements and peer training. Typically has 1–3 years of relevant experience.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technician III&lt;/strong&gt;: Performs complex mechanical assembly, integration, troubleshooting, and&amp;nbsp;testing with limited supervision. Serves as a technical resource for other technicians and&amp;nbsp;supports development hardware, environmental testing, flight readiness, and production&amp;nbsp;ramp. Typically has 3+ years of relevant experience or equivalent demonstrated proficiency.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Spacecraft or satellite mechanical assembly and integration&lt;br&gt;• Experience with primary and secondary spacecraft structures&lt;br&gt;• Mechanical mechanisms, deployment systems, hinges, latches, or release devices&lt;br&gt;• Precision alignment and dimensional inspection&lt;br&gt;• Torque application, safety wiring, staking, shimming, and mechanical fastening&lt;br&gt;• Structural bonding, potting, or adhesive application&lt;br&gt;• Experience supporting vibration, acoustic, thermal vacuum, or other environmental&amp;nbsp;testing&lt;br&gt;• Experience with lifting and handling flight hardware&lt;br&gt;• Familiarity with GD&amp;amp;T and mechanical inspection practices&lt;br&gt;• Experience with composite structures, lightweight materials, or additive-manufactured hardware&lt;br&gt;• Experience using coordinate measuring machines, laser trackers, optical tooling, or&amp;nbsp;other alignment equipment&lt;br&gt;• Relevant certifications in mechanical assembly, rigging, machining, composites, or&amp;nbsp;cleanroom operations&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COMPENSATION&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
