&lt;p&gt;True Anomaly is committed to equal employment opportunity on any basis protected by applicable state and federal laws. If you have a disability or additional need that requires accommodation, please do not hesitate to let us know.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To protect candidates and our company from application fraud and impersonation, we use third-party tools to verify applicant identity and detect fraudulent applications. Learn more in our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.trueanomaly.space/legal/privacy-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;Space is a warfighting domain. True Anomaly seeks those with the talent and ambition to build the technology that secures it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;OUR MISSION&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;True Anomaly delivers decisive capabilities for space superiority. We build autonomous spacecraft, advanced payloads, mission software, and space-based interceptors — enabling the U.S. and its Allies to secure the space environment and counter threats from the ultimate high ground.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;OUR VALUES&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be the offset.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;We create asymmetric advantages with creativity and ingenuity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What would it take?&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;We challenge assumptions to deliver ambitious results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;It’s the people.&lt;/strong&gt; Our team is our competitive advantage and we are better together.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;BENEFITS &amp;amp; PERKS&lt;/span&gt;*&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Best-in-class healthcare: &lt;/strong&gt;100% company-paid medical, dental, and vision coverage for you and your dependents, with HSA/HRA options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Generous time off: &lt;/strong&gt;Flexible Time Off (FTO) for exempt employees, accrued PTO of up to 25 days for non-exempt employees, plus 12 paid holidays; Parental Leave; Sick Leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fuel for your day: &lt;/strong&gt;Daily catered lunch and unlimited snacks for in-office employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;And more: &lt;/strong&gt;401(k) retirement plan, fitness reimbursement, and Dog Fridays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity participation: &lt;/strong&gt;Equity is included as part of our total compensation package, giving you an opportunity to share in the company’s success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*Do not apply to fixed term and temporary roles&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;YOUR MISSION&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Mission Architect to join our team in developing the next generation of missile defense systems. The Mission Architect will play a critical role in defining, analyzing, and ensuring the successful execution of missions across a system of systems. In this role, you will own the mission definition, mission-level trades, mission technical direction, and customer alignment throughout the full program execution lifecycle, from contract award through mission completion.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mission Design &amp;amp; Requirements Analysis:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with customers, stakeholders, and internal teams to define and document mission objectives, system requirements, and operational concepts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate customer and mission needs into actionable engineering solutions while ensuring alignment with technical and programmatic constraints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define key mission technical performance measures to establish a mission-driven decision-making framework.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply analysis and modeling techniques, including parametric analysis, to support engineering decisions in the absence of specific requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead system trade studies, performance evaluations, and feasibility assessments to ensure an optimal system architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, lead and execute engagement sequence and intercept analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform sensor, command-and-control, and interceptor integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design kill-chain and fire-control architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform system-of-systems performance modeling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare detailed technical reports, presentations, and documentation for internal and external stakeholders, including government agencies and customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;System Integration &amp;amp; Verification:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the integration of mission systems, ensuring seamless interaction among hardware, software, and operational components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop system-level integration and verification plans and conduct end-to-end testing to validate mission requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with subsystem teams to troubleshoot and resolve integration challenges, ensuring mission readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support mission operations teams during testing and real-time mission execution.&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Modeling, Simulation &amp;amp; Analysis:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply the fundamentals of astrodynamics using software and analysis tools, including orbit propagation, orbit determination, geometric orbit analysis, and mission engineering concepts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design parametric analyses and Monte Carlo studies to support engineering decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct system performance analyses, including assessments of reliability, safety, and mission effectiveness under various environmental conditions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess mission success criteria and operational risks and propose mitigation strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct pre-flight and post-flight mission analyses, including trajectory reconstruction and anomaly investigations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of experience in mission analysis, space operations, or orbital mechanics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical leadership and systems architecture experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of orbital mechanics, spacecraft dynamics, and autonomous space operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with mission analysis tools such as STK, FreeFlyer, GMAT, or similar software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in simulation tools and programming languages such as MATLAB, Python, or C++.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with mission planning and real-time mission support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must have or be able to obtain and maintain a TS/SCI or TS/SAP U.S. government security clearance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced degree in Aerospace, Mechanical, or Systems Engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active TS/SCI clearance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting defense or classified space missions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
