&lt;p&gt;*Do not apply to fixed term and temporary roles&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;YOUR MISSION&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Mission Security Administrator II, you will be responsible for the setup, configuration, maintenance, and day-to-day administration of national security space systems, classified ground-based Command and Control (C2) infrastructure, and engineering environments critical to our mission.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on operational role focused on implementing, maintaining, and administering classified systems, understanding and ensuring compliance requirements, and working face-to-face with customers daily. You will be the technical operator ensuring classified systems function reliably, remain compliant, and support mission objectives without interruption.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for candidates with practical experience broadly across the following areas:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;System administration (Windows/Linux server environments)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;User administration, identity, RBAC and software tool oversight&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cloud platform administration (AWS/Azure)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Patch management and configuration management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Software and hardware asset management, configuration management and documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Backup and disaster recovery operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work alongside Mission Security Engineers, IT professionals and cross-functional teams to operationalize security architecture, maintain Authorization to Operate (ATO) posture, and ensure classified systems remain operational and compliant with federal security standards. You will be a trusted operator responsible for the hands-on work that keeps mission systems secure and operational.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an ideal role for a security-focused system administrator with strong technical operational skills who thrives in a structured compliance environment and wants to support critical national security missions. If you take pride in maintaining secure, compliant, and reliable systems that protect lives and national interests, join our team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set up, configure, and maintain classified C2 systems, engineering environments, and supporting infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Administer and maintain Windows and Linux servers in classified environments, ensuring operational availability and security compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage user accounts, identities, role-based access controls (RBAC), and permissions across classified systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Configure and maintain cloud infrastructure in AWS or Azure, including IAM, networking, compute, and storage resources&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform routine system administration tasks including software installations, updates, patch management, and system troubleshooting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate software and hardware asset inventories, configuration baselines, and system documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute configuration management practices to ensure systems remain in compliance with approved baselines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform routine backup operations, verify backup integrity, and support disaster recovery testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support RMF compliance activities including evidence collection, documentation, and remediation tracking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remediate findings from vulnerability assessments, security audits, and compliance scans to maintain ATO posture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and maintain technical documentation including system configurations, user guides, standard operating procedures, and runbooks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide technical support and direct customer engagement to resolve system issues and respond to operational needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with government customers, ISSOs, ISSEs, and assessment teams during ATO and continuous monitoring activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in on-call rotation for system administration support and mission-critical system availability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active Secret clearance required (TS/SCI preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;DoD 8140 IAT Level II certification (Security+, CySA+, or equivalent) required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Education and experience requirement (one of the following):&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;◦ Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, Cybersecurity, or related field AND 2–4 years of experience in system administration, IT operations, or security operations&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;◦ Master&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, Cybersecurity, or related field (no experience required)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
