&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;BENEFITS &amp;amp; PERKS&lt;/span&gt;*&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Best-in-class healthcare: &lt;/strong&gt;100% company-paid medical, dental, and vision coverage for you and your dependents, with HSA/HRA options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Generous time off: &lt;/strong&gt;Flexible Time Off (FTO) for exempt employees, accrued PTO of up to 25 days for non-exempt employees, plus 12 paid holidays; Parental Leave; Sick Leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fuel for your day: &lt;/strong&gt;Daily catered lunch and unlimited snacks for in-office employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;And more: &lt;/strong&gt;401(k) retirement plan, fitness reimbursement, and Dog Fridays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity participation: &lt;/strong&gt;Equity is included as part of our total compensation package, giving you an opportunity to share in the company’s success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*Do not apply to fixed term and temporary roles&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;YOUR MISSION&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Network Engineer, you will design, operate, and optimize the enterprise network that powers True Anomaly’s engineering, manufacturing, and cloud-connected environments. You’ll work across complex on-prem topologies, hybrid cloud connectivity, and secure networking architectures to ensure reliability, performance, and scalability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll be joining a rapidly growing environment where your expertise will directly influence the stability and performance of our mission-critical infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect, deploy, and maintain enterprise network infrastructure including routing, switching, segmentation, VPN, and firewall services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate and support Palo Alto Networks firewalls and Juniper switching/routing platforms (or equivalent vendor experience).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain hybrid connectivity between on-prem environments and major cloud platforms (Azure, AWS, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot complex networking issues including routing loops, BGP/OSPF behavior, latency, packet loss, and inter-VLAN connectivity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage network performance, capacity planning, telemetry, and monitoring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement and maintain network security practices including segmentation and firewall rule hygiene.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support compliance-driven requirements aligned to CMMC and contribute to environments where ITAR or FedRAMP considerations may be present (not core to the role).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in an on-call rotation for critical network escalations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document architectures, change plans, diagrams, and runbooks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with infrastructure, security, DevOps, and cloud engineering teams in a high-velocity, fast-moving environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, or related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience as a Network Engineer supporting enterprise-class environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of routing/switching protocols (BGP, OSPF, VLANs, VRFs, STP, DNS, DHCP).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with firewalls (Palo Alto preferred) and routing/switching (Juniper preferred).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting hybrid or cloud-connected networks (Azure, AWS, or GCP).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong troubleshooting skills with packet captures, performance metrics, and logs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to thrive in a fast-paced, dynamic environment with shifting priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication, documentation, and cross-team collaboration skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with compliance-driven environments (CMMC, ITAR, FedRAMP) — helpful but not required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Availability to participate in an on-call rotation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active or previously held TS/SCI clearance (preferred but not required).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with security-focused networking architectures or compliance programs (CMMC, ITAR, FedRAMP).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Network automation or scripting experience (Python, Ansible, Terraform, or similar).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant certifications such as PCNSE, JNCIS/JNCIP, CCNP, or equivalent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with SD-WAN, multi-site networking, or data center architectures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in aerospace, defense, or high-security, compliance-heavy environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
