&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Principal Data Engineer to provide hands-on technical leadership in designing,&amp;nbsp;building&amp;nbsp;and evolving scalable data platforms. This role will&amp;nbsp;be responsible for&amp;nbsp;solving complex data engineering challenges,&amp;nbsp;establishing&amp;nbsp;engineering standards, and guiding the technical direction of True Anomaly’s Enterprise Data Platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate is a strong hands-on engineer with deep experience in Python, SQL, and modern cloud data platforms such as Snowflake, Databricks or Redshift.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will embrace the use of AI to aid data engineering and improve productivity, including leveraging AI-assisted development tools, automation and systems to accelerate pipeline development, improve code quality and optimize workflows.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, develop and maintain scalable data pipelines and data products using Python, SQL and modern data engineering practices, supporting batch, streaming, analytics, and AI/ML workloads&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and optimize ELT/ETL processes and data models using cloud data platforms with a focus on performance, scalability, reliability and cost efficiency&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and apply engineering best practices for data quality, testing, monitoring, observability, CI/CD, version control, security, and production reliability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own data engineering projects end-to-end, from technical design and development through deployment, production support, troubleshooting, and continuous improvement&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate across engineering, AI/ML, analytics, product and business teams to translate requirements into reliable, scalable data solutions and products and contribute to technical design decisions&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage AI-assisted engineering tools while contributing to data engineering technical excellence through code reviews, reusable frameworks, documentation, knowledge sharing, and mentoring other data engineers&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor Junior and Senior Data Engineers and&amp;nbsp;provide&amp;nbsp;technical guidance across the engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in data engineering and software engineering field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong hands-on Python and SQL experience&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience with Snowflake, Databricks, or both&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of data engineering, data architecture, data&amp;nbsp;modelling&amp;nbsp;and ELT/ETL&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of software engineering practices including Git, testing, CI/CD&amp;nbsp;and code reviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to provide technical leadership and mentor other engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adopt AI-assisted engineering tools to improve productivity and delivery speed&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with AWS,&amp;nbsp;Azure&amp;nbsp;or GCP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Airflow,&amp;nbsp;dbt, Kafka or similar technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building out Lakehouse architectures&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with data governance,&amp;nbsp;lineage&amp;nbsp;and observability&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;What we are looking for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on Principal level engineering role. The successful candidate should be comfortable writing code, designing architecture, solving&amp;nbsp;difficult technical problems, and influencing best data practices across the company&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COMPENSATION&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Base Salary: &lt;/strong&gt;Denver - $200,000 - $280,000, Long Beach - $210,000 - $290,000&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity + Benefits&lt;/strong&gt; including Health, Dental, Vision, HRA/HSA options, PTO and paid holidays, 401K, Parental Leave&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Your actual level and base salary will be&amp;nbsp;determined on a case-by-case basis and may vary based on the following considerations: job-related knowledge and skills, education, location, and experience.&lt;/em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
