&lt;p&gt;As a Principal RF Electrical Engineer at True Anomaly, you will set the functional RF architecture strategy for the company and be accountable for enterprise-wide technical decisions across all spacecraft communication systems. You will shape the long-term technical direction of the RF discipline, influence company leadership, grow senior engineering talent, and represent True Anomaly&#39;s capabilities externally to customers, partners, and the broader aerospace community.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect multi-mission RF systems across S/X/Ka-Band and other frequency regimes; ensure end-to-end link margin and performance robustness across the enterprise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define mission communication architectures; validate end-to-end RF system performance at program and enterprise levels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee mission-level RF verification and payload qualification across multiple concurrent programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define corporate EMI/EMC strategy; engage with regulatory bodies and spectrum authorities on behalf of True Anomaly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the long-term communication system strategy and link design philosophy across all programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shapes company RF technical narratives; influence executives and senior leadership on strategic technical pursuits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Grow and shape the senior RF engineering talent pipeline; mentor staff and senior engineers into leadership roles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive transformative solutions that establish new RF capabilities at the company level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define enterprise delivery standards and drive consistent outcomes across the RF organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as an external representative for True Anomaly&#39;s RF capabilities at industry forums, with customers, and with partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Embody and scale True Anomaly&#39;s engineering values company-wide; set the cultural and technical tone for the RF discipline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Electrical Engineering or related field (Master&#39;s or PhD strongly preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;14+ years of progressive RF engineering experience, including significant experience in spacecraft or space-borne communication systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated track record of architecting and delivering multi-mission, multi-band RF communication systems in space or missile defense applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise across the full RF engineering stack: component expertise, subsystem architecture, link analysis, EMI/EMC, test and qualification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience engaging with regulatory bodies, spectrum authorities, or standards organizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to influence at the executive level and drive enterprise-wide technical strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong track record of growing and developing senior engineering talent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with classified space communication systems and NSA Type 1 encryption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in satellite communication link optimization and technology trades&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Awareness of key technology progression across the industry as it pertains to forward looking implementation and strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with regulatory filing committees and ITU/FCC spectrum coordination processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Publications, patents, or conference presentations in RF/microwave engineering or space communications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a high-growth aerospace startup environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Record of external industry influence through panels, working groups, or advisory roles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
