&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TextRun SCXW267002851 BCX0&quot; lang=&quot;EN-US&quot; data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW267002851 BCX0&quot;&gt;This position will be open until it is successfully filled. To &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW267002851 BCX0&quot;&gt;submit&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW267002851 BCX0&quot;&gt; your application, please follow the directions below.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TextRun MacChromeBold SCXW267002851 BCX0&quot; lang=&quot;EN-US&quot; data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW267002851 BCX0&quot;&gt;#LI-Onsite&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;To conform to U.S. Government space technology export regulations, including the International Traffic in Arms Regulations (ITAR) you must be a U.S. citizen, lawful permanent resident of the U.S., protected individual as defined by 8 U.S.C. 1324b(a)(3), or eligible to obtain the required authorizations from the U.S. Department of State.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;True Anomaly is committed to equal employment opportunity on any basis protected by applicable state and federal laws. If you have a disability or additional need that requires accommodation, please do not hesitate to let us know.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To protect candidates and our company from application fraud and impersonation, we use third-party tools to verify applicant identity and detect fraudulent applications. Learn more in our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.trueanomaly.space/legal/privacy-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;Space is a warfighting domain. True Anomaly seeks those with the talent and ambition to build the technology that secures it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;OUR MISSION&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;True Anomaly delivers decisive capabilities for space superiority. We build autonomous spacecraft, advanced payloads, mission software, and space-based interceptors — enabling the U.S. and its Allies to secure the space environment and counter threats from the ultimate high ground.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;OUR VALUES&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be the offset.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;We create asymmetric advantages with creativity and ingenuity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What would it take?&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;We challenge assumptions to deliver ambitious results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;It’s the people.&lt;/strong&gt; Our team is our competitive advantage and we are better together.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;BENEFITS &amp;amp; PERKS&lt;/span&gt;*&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Best-in-class healthcare: &lt;/strong&gt;100% company-paid medical, dental, and vision coverage for you and your dependents, with HSA/HRA options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Generous time off: &lt;/strong&gt;Flexible Time Off (FTO) for exempt employees, accrued PTO of up to 25 days for non-exempt employees, plus 12 paid holidays; Parental Leave; Sick Leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fuel for your day: &lt;/strong&gt;Daily catered lunch and unlimited snacks for in-office employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;And more: &lt;/strong&gt;401(k) retirement plan, fitness reimbursement, and Dog Fridays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity participation: &lt;/strong&gt;Equity is included as part of our total compensation package, giving you an opportunity to share in the company’s success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*Do not apply to fixed term and temporary roles&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;YOUR MISSION&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a Senior Mechanical Assembly Integration &amp;amp; Test Technician to support mechanical assembly, integration, and environmental test operations for component and system level hardware. This role is split between hands on mechanical integration, installing mechanical components, building sub-assemblies, and supporting build activities, and environmental test operations, including component-level and thermal vacuum (TVAC) testing. The ideal candidate has 8+ years of experience across mechanical build/integration and test, with strong hands-on experience maintaining vibration (vibe) tables and TVAC chambers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Mechanical Integration &amp;amp; Assembly&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Install mechanical components and build sub-assemblies per engineering drawings, work instructions, and travelers&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Perform mechanical assembly, integration, and disassembly of components, subsystems, and system-level hardware&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Fabricate, install, and align test fixtures and ground support equipment (GSE)&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Support build activities during down time between test campaigns, including fit checks, hardware prep, and staging&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Work closely with engineering to resolve fit, tolerance, or build issues during integration&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Test Operations &amp;amp; Facility Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Set up, operate, and support component level environmental testing, including vibration, shock,and thermal vacuum (TVAC) testing&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Perform preventive and corrective maintenance, calibration support, and troubleshooting on vibration tables/shakers and TVAC chambers&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Install and connect test instrumentation (accelerometers, thermocouples, etc.) and support data acquisition setup&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Support facility upkeep, including LN2/GN2 systems, vacuum pumps, and chamber controllers&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Troubleshoot equipment issues and resolve hardware/test anomalies during live test operations&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Other&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Follow and help refine procedures, travelers, and work instructions, document results, anomalies, and non-conformances&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Maintain calibration records and equipment logs for test facility compliance&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Mentor junior technicians on assembly, integration, and test practices&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Adhere to cleanroom protocols, ESD handling requirements, and safety procedures at all times&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;•&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; High school diploma or equivalent required; Associate&#39;s degree or technical certification in a relevant field preferred&lt;br&gt;•&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; 8+ years of hands-on experience in mechanical integration, assembly, and test, including:&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;•&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Mechanical component installation and sub-assembly build&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Component-level environmental testing&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;•&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Thermal vacuum (TVAC) testing&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Vibration testing (sine, random, shock)&lt;br&gt;•&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Demonstrated hands on experience performing maintenance, troubleshooting, and calibration support on vibration tables/shakers and TVAC chambers&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Proficiency reading and interpreting engineering drawings, schematics, and work instructions&lt;br&gt;•&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Experience with precision hand tools, torque tools, and mechanical assembly techniques&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Familiarity with test equipment such as chamber controllers, vacuum systems, data acquisition systems, and shaker controllers&lt;br&gt;•&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Strong collaboration skills with the ability to work effectively across cross-functional teams including Engineering, Quality, Test, and Supply chain.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;•&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Ability to accurately document build activities, test setups, and anomalies&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Experience in aerospace, defense, or satellite hardware environments&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Familiarity with cleanroom protocols and ESD-sensitive handling&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Experience with cryogenic systems (LN2) and high/low vacuum systems&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Forklift, crane, or hoist certification&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Experience mentoring or leading junior technicians&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Physical Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Ability to lift up to 40 lbs&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Ability to work in cleanroom and lab environments, including exposure to cryogenic materials and vacuum systems&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Willingness to work flexible hours during test campaigns, including occasional off-shift or weekend work as needed&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Ability to stand, kneel, and work in confined spaces for extended periods as needed&lt;/p&gt;
