&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;Space is a warfighting domain. True Anomaly seeks those with the talent and ambition to build the technology that secures it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;OUR MISSION&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;True Anomaly delivers decisive capabilities for space superiority. We build autonomous spacecraft, advanced payloads, mission software, and space-based interceptors — enabling the U.S. and its Allies to secure the space environment and counter threats from the ultimate high ground.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;OUR VALUES&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be the offset.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;We create asymmetric advantages with creativity and ingenuity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What would it take?&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;We challenge assumptions to deliver ambitious results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;It’s the people.&lt;/strong&gt; Our team is our competitive advantage and we are better together.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;BENEFITS &amp;amp; PERKS&lt;/span&gt;*&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Best-in-class healthcare: &lt;/strong&gt;100% company-paid medical, dental, and vision coverage for you and your dependents, with HSA/HRA options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Generous time off: &lt;/strong&gt;Flexible Time Off (FTO) for exempt employees, accrued PTO of up to 25 days for non-exempt employees, plus 12 paid holidays; Parental Leave; Sick Leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fuel for your day: &lt;/strong&gt;Daily catered lunch and unlimited snacks for in-office employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;And more: &lt;/strong&gt;401(k) retirement plan, fitness reimbursement, and Dog Fridays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity participation: &lt;/strong&gt;Equity is included as part of our total compensation package, giving you an opportunity to share in the company’s success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*Do not apply to fixed term and temporary roles&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;YOUR MISSION&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Communication Designer turns complex, often sensitive technology into stories people can understand, remember, and act on. You will work with Communications, Business Development, engineers, and executives to find what matters, structure the story, and design presentations that are clear, distinctive, and unmistakably True Anomaly. The work spans capability and company presentations, customer briefings, business development materials, executive communications, and keynotes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on design role for someone with a strong creative point of view and meticulous craft. You will bring ideas for how a story looks, feels, and unfolds, using visual concepts, imagery, and thoughtful pacing to make ideas resonate. You will find the headline and make sure that comes through clearly. You will follow our brand guidelines, and when a project needs something, the system doesn’t have yet, you will help create it and expand its possibilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Story and Message&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with subject matter experts to pull the essential ideas out of conversations, technical documents, data, and rough source material. Ask good questions and identify gaps and find unexpected connections or perspectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Communications and Business Development to stay on message. They own the message; you help structure it, sequence it, and find the clearest way to show it. Support copy as needed and bring in copywriters for larger needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Validate technical content with its owners. Explain your decisions and challenge approaches that obscure the point.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Design&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop visual concepts that give each presentation a creative approach. Use typography, composition, pacing, and hierarchy to build a story across slides. Create diagrams, charts, and timelines that clarify technical concepts without losing accuracy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create original graphics and integrate photography, renders, illustration, video, and motion from internal teams and outside partners. Identify missing assets and help define them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adapt depth and structure for technical briefings, executive discussions, customer meetings, live presentations, and materials meant to be read alone.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work confidently within our brand system. When a project or story calls for a new approach, develop in partnership with Brand &amp;amp; Creative leadership so the work expands the system’s creative range.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build editable templates and asset libraries that non-designers can use with confidence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Sensitive Information and Delivery&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handle proprietary and export-controlled content according to company policy, including marking, review, storage, and sharing. Raise questions early.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with Business Development, and with Finance and People teams, who are frequent end users of our presentations and templates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Carry projects from intake through delivery, checking content, labels, sources, formatting, and files. Manage multiple projects and communicate tradeoffs clearly. Support live delivery for executive and keynote presentations as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in communication, presentation, information, or brand design, with substantial presentation work and a record of leading complex, high-visibility projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A portfolio that shows excellent visual craft and the ability to turn complex or incomplete information into a clear, persuasive story. A portfolio link is required. Where possible, show the starting material alongside the finished work and explain your specific contribution. Anonymized or redacted examples are welcome.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong editorial judgment: you can identify the main point and decide what to emphasize, simplify, sequence, or cut.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working directly with technical experts, senior stakeholders, and business development or sales teams, including developing the narrative before design begins.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience handling sensitive, proprietary, or controlled information, or the discipline to learn quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent typography, layout, data visualization, and diagramming skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing within an established brand system, creating new components when needed, and building reusable templates for non-designers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced proficiency in PowerPoint, Adobe Creative Cloud, and Figma, including editable charts, master layouts, and reliable file handoff.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort in a fast-moving environment where the function and workflows are still being built.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Valuable but not required: aerospace, defense, or other complex technical experience; keynote, launch, or capability storytelling; motion and video integration; creating guidance that helps teams adopt new tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Genuine interest in aerospace, defense, or national security. Domain expertise isn’t required; taking the mission seriously is.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COMPENSATION&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-leveltext=&quot;&quot; data-font=&quot;Symbol&quot; data-listid=&quot;2&quot; data-list-defn-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335552541&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:720,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:360,&amp;quot;469769226&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;Symbol&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469769242&amp;quot;:[8226],&amp;quot;469777803&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;left&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777804&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777815&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;hybridMultilevel&amp;quot;}&quot; data-aria-posinset=&quot;1&quot; data-aria-level=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Base Salary:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:160,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt; $105,000 - $205,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
