&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;Space is a warfighting domain. True Anomaly seeks those with the talent and ambition to build the technology that secures it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;OUR MISSION&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;True Anomaly delivers decisive capabilities for space superiority. We build autonomous spacecraft, advanced payloads, mission software, and space-based interceptors — enabling the U.S. and its Allies to secure the space environment and counter threats from the ultimate high ground.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;OUR VALUES&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be the offset.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;We create asymmetric advantages with creativity and ingenuity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What would it take?&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;We challenge assumptions to deliver ambitious results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;It’s the people.&lt;/strong&gt; Our team is our competitive advantage and we are better together.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;BENEFITS &amp;amp; PERKS&lt;/span&gt;*&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Best-in-class healthcare: &lt;/strong&gt;100% company-paid medical, dental, and vision coverage for you and your dependents, with HSA/HRA options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Generous time off: &lt;/strong&gt;Flexible Time Off (FTO) for exempt employees, accrued PTO of up to 25 days for non-exempt employees, plus 12 paid holidays; Parental Leave; Sick Leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fuel for your day: &lt;/strong&gt;Daily catered lunch and unlimited snacks for in-office employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;And more: &lt;/strong&gt;401(k) retirement plan, fitness reimbursement, and Dog Fridays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity participation: &lt;/strong&gt;Equity is included as part of our total compensation package, giving you an opportunity to share in the company’s success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*Do not apply to fixed term and temporary roles&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;YOUR MISSION&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Senior Environmental Graphic Designer, you&#39;ll define how True Anomaly shows up in the physical world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a ground-floor opportunity to establish the physical expression of a brand at a company in tremendous growth, creating the environmental design language for an entire industry being defined in real time. Our brand increasingly lives beyond the screen: in workplaces and R&amp;amp;D environments, customer spaces, industry events, and installations that make what we&#39;re building real.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll bring both a designer&#39;s and a curator&#39;s eye to the work, considering how graphics, language, imagery, objects, materials, and architecture work together to tell a story. The goal isn&#39;t to apply the brand to an environment but to make our technology, people, and mission tangible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll sit within Brand &amp;amp; Creative, reporting to the Head of Graphic Design &amp;amp; Brand Identity, and partner closely with Facilities Design, Experiential, and Copy. Your work will span permanent architectural environments and quick experiential projects.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll start hands-on, shaping both the work and the systems behind it. As True Anomaly grows, you&#39;ll define how environmental design grows as a capability within Brand &amp;amp; Creative.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Design &amp;amp; Storytelling&lt;br&gt;• Lead environmental graphic design from concept through installation across workplaces, R&amp;amp;D spaces,&amp;nbsp;customer environments, events, exhibits, and branded installations&lt;br&gt;• Translate True Anomaly&#39;s visual identity into physical space, creating new expressions of typography,&amp;nbsp;imagery, information, materiality, and storytelling rather than applying existing assets to surfaces&lt;br&gt;• Bring an editorial point of view to physical environments, composing graphics, imagery, artifacts, objects,&amp;nbsp;and digital content into cohesive spatial narratives&lt;br&gt;• Develop design deliverables that clearly communicate intent: concepts, mood boards, layouts, elevations,&amp;nbsp;material palettes, mockups, presentations&lt;br&gt;• Design experiences that integrate physical and digital storytelling through displays, projection, motion,&amp;nbsp;interactive content, and product models&lt;br&gt;• Translate complex technology and ideas into experiences that are compelling and understandable without&amp;nbsp;oversimplifying&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;Experience &amp;amp; Execution&lt;br&gt;• Design branded environments for events, launches, customer demos, and installations, from scalable&amp;nbsp;systems to bespoke moments, in partnership with internal teams and external agencies&lt;br&gt;• Consider the full audience journey: what draws someone in, what they discover, and what they remember&lt;br&gt;• Create flexible design systems that scale across different footprints, venues, audiences, and budgets&amp;nbsp;without losing brand integrity&lt;br&gt;• Support on-site installation, styling, troubleshooting, and final creative decisions when needed&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;Production &amp;amp; Implementation&lt;br&gt;• Own environmental design through production and installation, ensuring creative intent survives fabrication&amp;nbsp;realities&lt;br&gt;• Prepare and review production documentation: artwork, dimensions, elevations, specifications, material&amp;nbsp;selections, shop drawings, installation guides&lt;br&gt;• Partner directly with fabricators, printers, sign vendors, architects, contractors, and experiential agencies&lt;br&gt;• Evaluate materials, substrates, finishes, fabrication techniques, and physical details for quality, durability,&amp;nbsp;cost, and feasibility&lt;br&gt;• Participate in site surveys, production reviews, installation oversight, and punch-listing as needed&lt;br&gt;• Understand schedules and budgets well enough to make smart creative decisions and identify risks early&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;Build the Environmental Brand System&lt;br&gt;• Define True Anomaly&#39;s environmental design language as an extension of the visual identity, creating&amp;nbsp;continuity across digital, print, motion, and environmental expressions&lt;br&gt;• Establish principles, standards, templates, material approaches, and repeatable systems that enable&amp;nbsp;consistent execution without one-size-fits-all solutions&lt;br&gt;• Develop guidelines and tools that enable internal teams and external partners to execute the environmental&amp;nbsp;brand&lt;br&gt;• Build and maintain relationships with a trusted network of fabricators, printers, vendors, craftspeople, and&amp;nbsp;specialty partners&lt;br&gt;• Continue exploring new materials, technologies, and fabrication methods that push the physical expression&amp;nbsp;of the brand forward and raise the quality bar as the company grows&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;p-pdf_iframe__page&quot; data-page-number=&quot;2&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;textLayer&quot; data-main-rotation=&quot;0&quot;&gt;• 6+ years of experience in environmental graphic design, experiential design, exhibition design, branded environments, or a closely related discipline.&lt;br&gt;• A portfolio demonstrating exceptional environmental and graphic design across physical spaces. Experience spanning workplace, exhibitions, cultural spaces, events, retail, hospitality, or other branded environments is relevant.&lt;br&gt;• Strong graphic design fundamentals, particularly typography, composition, hierarchy, imagery, and identity systems.&lt;br&gt;• A strong editorial and curatorial sensibility, with an ability to combine graphics, language, imagery, objects, technology, and space into a coherent narrative.&lt;br&gt;• Experience taking environmental projects from concept through fabrication and installation.&lt;br&gt;• Fluency in large-format print production, signage, materials, finishes, substrates, fabrication techniques, and installation methods.&lt;br&gt;• Comfortable reading and reviewing architectural plans, elevations, shop drawings, details, and specifications.&lt;br&gt;• Experience working directly with fabricators, printers, architects, contractors, experiential agencies, and other external partners.&lt;br&gt;• Proficiency in Adobe Creative Suite and Figma. Working knowledge of CAD, SketchUp, Rhino, or other&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;textLayer&quot; data-main-rotation=&quot;0&quot;&gt;spatial design and visualization tools is a plus.&lt;br&gt;• Ability to communicate spatial ideas clearly through sketches, diagrams, elevations, renderings, mockups, and presentations.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;textLayer&quot; data-main-rotation=&quot;0&quot;&gt;• Strong creative judgment paired with the resourcefulness to solve design problems within real-world budget, schedule, production, and site constraints.&lt;br&gt;• Comfortable moving between highly visible, long-term environments and fast-turn projects without treating either as a lesser design problem.&lt;br&gt;• Collaborative by nature and comfortable developing ideas alongside graphic designers, experiential designers, writers, content creators, architects, and production partners.&lt;br&gt;• Curious about technology, culture, design, architecture, art, and the world beyond traditional environmental graphic design.&lt;br&gt;• Able to operate with autonomy in a fast-moving environment, balancing multiple projects at different scales and stages of development.&lt;br&gt;• Willingness to travel for site visits, events, production reviews, and installations as needed.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
