&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;Space is a warfighting domain. True Anomaly seeks those with the talent and ambition to build the technology that secures it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;OUR MISSION&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;True Anomaly delivers decisive capabilities for space superiority. We build autonomous spacecraft, advanced payloads, mission software, and space-based interceptors — enabling the U.S. and its Allies to secure the space environment and counter threats from the ultimate high ground.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;OUR VALUES&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be the offset.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;We create asymmetric advantages with creativity and ingenuity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What would it take?&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;We challenge assumptions to deliver ambitious results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;It’s the people.&lt;/strong&gt; Our team is our competitive advantage and we are better together.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;BENEFITS &amp;amp; PERKS&lt;/span&gt;*&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Best-in-class healthcare: &lt;/strong&gt;100% company-paid medical, dental, and vision coverage for you and your dependents, with HSA/HRA options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Generous time off: &lt;/strong&gt;Flexible Time Off (FTO) for exempt employees, accrued PTO of up to 25 days for non-exempt employees, plus 12 paid holidays; Parental Leave; Sick Leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fuel for your day: &lt;/strong&gt;Daily catered lunch and unlimited snacks for in-office employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;And more: &lt;/strong&gt;401(k) retirement plan, fitness reimbursement, and Dog Fridays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity participation: &lt;/strong&gt;Equity is included as part of our total compensation package, giving you an opportunity to share in the company’s success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*Do not apply to fixed term and temporary roles&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;YOUR MISSION&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Modeling and simulation is how True Anomaly turns operational problems into engineering decisions. Before a spacecraft flies or an interceptor engages, our simulations tell us whether the architecture will work, how it will perform against a thinking adversary, and where the margins really are. True Anomaly is seeking a Modeling &amp;amp; Simulation Engineer to build and run the mission- and engagement-level simulations that drive design, concept-of-operations, and acquisition decisions across our space and missile defense portfolio.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work in a fast-paced, interdisciplinary team to model threats, sensors, spacecraft, interceptors, and command-and-control (C2) systems. This role focuses on building credible, validated simulation environments and turning their results into clear recommendations for engineers, program leadership, and government customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain physics-based models for space and missile defense mission analysis, including:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Threat trajectories, including ballistic, hypersonic, maneuvering, and on-orbit threats&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Space-based and terrestrial sensors (electro-optical/infrared, radar, RF), including detection, tracking, and discrimination performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interceptor and spacecraft kinematics, guidance, navigation, and control (GNC), and engagement geometry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rendezvous and proximity operations (RPO), orbit determination, and space domain awareness (SDA)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communications links, data latency, and C2/battle management decision logic&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build engagement- and mission-level simulations that tie these models together for end-to-end kill-chain analysis (detect, track, target, engage, assess)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate models into digital engineering, software-in-the-loop (SIL), hardware-in-the-loop (HIL), and distributed simulation environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and execute model verification, validation, and accreditation (VV&amp;amp;A), and correlate simulation results with test and flight data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop analysis tooling, automation, and visualization in Python and C++&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with systems, GNC, payload, software, and flight-test engineers to support requirements development, test planning, and verification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in code reviews, architectural discussions, and sprint planning sessions to maintain high standards of quality and adherence to project timelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run Monte Carlo, sensitivity, and trade studies, and brief results to internal and government stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in aerospace engineering, mechanical engineering, electrical engineering, physics, applied mathematics, computer science, a similar discipline, or relevant experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of professional experience in modeling and simulation, mission analysis, or aerospace/defense systems engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience modeling at least one of the following:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ballistic, hypersonic, or maneuvering threats&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Space-based interceptors or kinetic and non-kinetic engagement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;EO/IR, radar, or RF sensor phenomenology and tracking/fusion algorithms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spacecraft attitude, orbit determination, and RPO&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;C2, battle management, and weapon-target assignment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Python and C++ for model development and data analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of orbital mechanics, flight dynamics, or missile/interceptor trajectories&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, including presenting technical results to non-specialist audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent problem-solving skills and attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Monte Carlo methods, statistical analysis, and data visualization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;U.S. Citizen and eligible for DoD Secret or TS/SCI clearance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active DoD Secret or TS/SCI clearance; SAP eligibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting space or missile defense programs (e.g., MDA, SDA, Space Systems Command, Golden Dome)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of numerical methods:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ODE solvers and integration schemes (Runge-Kutta, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Estimation and filtering (Kalman filters, batch least squares)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimization and design of experiments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with 6DOF simulation and GNC algorithm analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with uncertainty quantification and model VV&amp;amp;A&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with version control systems (Git) and CI/CD pipelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
