&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;Space is a warfighting domain. True Anomaly seeks those with the talent and ambition to build the technology that secures it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;OUR MISSION&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;True Anomaly delivers decisive capabilities for space superiority. We build autonomous spacecraft, advanced payloads, mission software, and space-based interceptors — enabling the U.S. and its Allies to secure the space environment and counter threats from the ultimate high ground.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;OUR VALUES&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be the offset.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;We create asymmetric advantages with creativity and ingenuity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What would it take?&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;We challenge assumptions to deliver ambitious results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;It’s the people.&lt;/strong&gt; Our team is our competitive advantage and we are better together.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;BENEFITS &amp;amp; PERKS&lt;/span&gt;*&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Best-in-class healthcare: &lt;/strong&gt;100% company-paid medical, dental, and vision coverage for you and your dependents, with HSA/HRA options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Generous time off: &lt;/strong&gt;Flexible Time Off (FTO) for exempt employees, accrued PTO of up to 25 days for non-exempt employees, plus 12 paid holidays; Parental Leave; Sick Leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fuel for your day: &lt;/strong&gt;Daily catered lunch and unlimited snacks for in-office employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;And more: &lt;/strong&gt;401(k) retirement plan, fitness reimbursement, and Dog Fridays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity participation: &lt;/strong&gt;Equity is included as part of our total compensation package, giving you an opportunity to share in the company’s success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*Do not apply to fixed term and temporary roles&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;YOUR MISSION&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Staff RF Electrical Engineer at True Anomaly, you will define the architecture for full spacecraft RF systems and be accountable for program-level communication system outcomes across multiple teams. You will develop reusable engineering tools and standards, drive cross-organizational alignment, and serve as a technical coach who builds the next generation of RF engineers at True Anomaly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define architecture for full spacecraft RF systems; establish design and performance standards across programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop system-level RF performance tools, analysis models, and standard methodologies used across the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish standardized RF test methods; resolve cross-system EMI/EMC issues that span multiple subsystems or programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimize RF architectures at the system level; inform and lead complex trade studies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run multi-stream RF projects; coordinate across engineering teams to deliver program-level outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide technical mentorship and coaching to engineers across teams; develop durable engineering practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape cross-organizational technical alignment; communicate clearly under pressure and ambiguity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support subcontracts and supplier development through design, development, and procurement efforts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Embed True Anomaly&#39;s engineering values into cross-org delivery; serve as a visible role model for technical excellence and accountability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Electrical Engineering or related field (Master&#39;s or PhD preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10–14 years of experience in RF system design and development for aerospace applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience defining RF system/payload architectures for spacecraft programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in link budget analysis, antenna systems, EMC/EMI, and space communication protocols&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading multi-team technical programs and driving cross-functional delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced proficiency in RF simulation and analysis tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong leadership and communication skills; ability to influence and align without direct authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with S/X/Ka-Band communications systems for space applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in satellite communication link optimization and technology trades&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with software-defined radios (SDRs) at the system architecture level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with regulatory spectrum filing and frequency coordination&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with RF missile defense applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with encryption algorithms (NSA Type 1 preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of developing junior and mid-level engineers into senior contributors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a startup or high-growth aerospace environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
